NAME
randbit ‐ generate cryptographically secure random bits

SYNOPSIS
randbit [MODE] [ARGS...]

DESCRIPTION
randbit generates cryptographically secure random values using
the operating system's random number generator.

MODES
No mode
Output a random bit (0 or 1).

```
-b, --bool
    Output "true" or "false".

-c, --coin
    Output "Heads" or "Tails".

-i, --int
    Output a random signed 32-bit integer.

-u, --uint
    Output a random unsigned 32-bit integer.

-s, --bitstream
    Output a random 32-bit value as a bit stream.

-l, --label [0] [1]
    Output one of the two supplied labels, corresponding to
    random bit values 0 and 1.

-v, --version
    Show version information.

-h, --help
    Show help.
```

EXIT STATUS
0   Success.
1   Too many arguments.
2   Too few arguments.
3   Invalid arguments.
4   Random number generation failed.

EXAMPLES
randbit

```
randbit --bool

randbit --coin

randbit --int

randbit --uint

randbit --bitstream

randbit --label SHA-256 SHA-3-256
```

